ee cash flow, or 7% after stock compensation.","ROE of 44% is amplified by 3.8x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 14.8% of revenue on R&D and 5.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.8x net debt to EBITDA ($1.9B of cash against $6.7B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 9.3x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 6.7, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.3% over 3 years, 1.6% over 5 years and 2.6% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 17%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -5.7% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 34%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.2x, 4.7% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 9, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 10.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 96%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (32 sales, net $8.0M sold).","It returns 5.4% a year to shareholders (4.4% in buybacks and 1.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 5.8% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 12,300 employees, each generates about $902K of revenue, 2.4x the Consumer Cyclical median.","That works out to $117K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.9M (5x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (8/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $49K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":61,"head":"Avoid: priced 289% above its fair value of $31.33.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 40, gates 11/26)","ROIC 18.1% vs WACC 9.0%","FCF margin 12.9%","Altman Z in the safe zone","12-1 month momentum +34%"],"co